(go/type Config "Config holds configuration for HTTP proxy settings. See\nFromEnvironment for details.\n" (struct



    ^{:line 32 :tag string :doc "HTTPProxy represents the value of the HTTP_PROXY or\nhttp_proxy environment variable. It will be used as the proxy\nURL for HTTP requests unless overridden by NoProxy.\n"} HTTPProxy




    ^{:line 37 :tag string :doc "HTTPSProxy represents the HTTPS_PROXY or https_proxy\nenvironment variable. It will be used as the proxy URL for\nHTTPS requests unless overridden by NoProxy.\n"} HTTPSProxy














    ^{:line 52 :tag string :doc "NoProxy represents the NO_PROXY or no_proxy environment\nvariable. It specifies a string that contains comma-separated values\nspecifying hosts that should be excluded from proxying. Each value is\nrepresented by an IP address prefix (1.2.3.4), an IP address prefix in\nCIDR notation (1.2.3.4/8), a domain name, or a special DNS label (*).\nAn IP address prefix and domain name can also include a literal port\nnumber (1.2.3.4:80).\nA domain name matches that name and all subdomains. A domain name with\na leading \".\" matches subdomains only. For example \"foo.com\" matches\n\"foo.com\" and \"bar.foo.com\"; \".y.com\" matches \"x.y.com\" but not \"y.com\".\nA single asterisk (*) indicates that no proxying should be done.\nA best effort is made to parse the string and errors are\nignored.\n"} NoProxy







    ^{:line 60 :tag bool :doc "CGI holds whether the current process is running\nas a CGI handler (FromEnvironment infers this from the\npresence of a REQUEST_METHOD environment variable).\nWhen this is set, ProxyForURL will return an error\nwhen HTTPProxy applies, because a client could be\nsetting HTTP_PROXY maliciously. See https://go.dev/s/cgihttpproxy.\n"} CGI))



